# Pairs with DelegationsDisjoint. The registry registers a receiver delegation
# for a txid it already delegates as an authoring sub-saga, which is what it
# would do without TxRegistryGrain.ThrowIfWouldCoexist (issue #2353). The
# public apply seam trusts the origin a caller supplies, so the registry's own
# check is the only thing that keeps the two maps disjoint for a txid the
# origin cluster is handed back.
MODULE: DelegationsDisjointRegistryAdmitsForeignClaim
TARGET: DelegationsDisjoint
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the registry admits a receiver delegation for a txid it already delegates as an authoring sub-saga
PERTURBS: ForeignOriginClaim

--- FIND
    /\ orcv' = IF oext[tr] THEN orcv ELSE [orcv EXCEPT ![tr] = TRUE]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no coexistence check.
    /\ orcv' = [orcv EXCEPT ![tr] = TRUE]
--- END
